    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d407">

                <pb facs="0378" n="368" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg368"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894A.00/7–2749</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by Mr. Livingston T.
                            Merchant, of the Office of Far Eastern Affairs, to the Chief
                        of the Division of Chinese Affairs</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sprouse</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1949-08-03">August 3, 1949</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I return herewith for CA’s files FE’s Secret memorandum of July 27, 1949 to the
                    Secretary regarding an approach to Ambassador Koo and attaching an <hi
                        rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> on the subject of Taiwan.</p>
                <p>Mr. Rusk originally approved this for submission to the Secretary but at a
                    meeting on August 2 with Mr. Kennan, Mr. Rusk, Mr. Butterworth and myself it was
                    finally agreed that it would be unwise to make this <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >démarche</hi> in the teeth of the publication of the White Paper.<anchor
                        n="92" xml:id="d407-f1"/> I presume the appropriate resting place for the
                    effort is now the files.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>L[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ivingston</hi>] T. M[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">erchant</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d407-f1" n="92" xml:id="d407-f1-content">
                <p>For correspondence regarding publication of the White Paper, see <ref
                        target="#pg1365">pp. 1365</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
